# Store all text as LF and check it out as LF on every platform, so the
# working tree is identical on Linux CI, GitHub's Windows runners (whose git
# defaults to core.autocrlf=true), and local clones. Biome enforces LF; a
# CRLF checkout makes `biome check` fail.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-native scripts run under cmd.exe; keep CRLF on checkout.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binaries: never normalize.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.jar binary
